      grammarExamples:<String>["Having examined the evidence, the panel reopened the discussion.","Faced with competing accounts, the researchers requested a second review.","The witnesses, questioned independently, offered different explanations."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on contested museum ownership, Dr. Salma, the provenance curator, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A family demanded that a ceremonial vessel be removed from public display. A handwritten shipping register named two incompatible donors. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. A cultural association argued that a legal bill of sale could not establish informed consent. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Salma asked independent researchers to reconstruct the acquisition chronology. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The trustees suspended exhibition captions until the unresolved claims could be explained. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
      listeningQuestion:"What principle guided Dr. Salma's response to the dispute?",
      listeningOptions:<String>["Publish the most dramatic interpretation immediately","Distinguish verified evidence from unresolved interpretations","Exclude every stakeholder who disagrees"],
