      grammarExamples:<String>["The assessment of scientific risk communication required sustained scrutiny.","A revision of the criteria improved procedural fairness.","The disclosure of uncertainty strengthened the argument."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on scientific risk communication, Dr. Amir, the climate scientist, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. An early projection was reported as a certain prediction of coastal flooding. The confidence intervals widened when a missing tidal series was restored. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Municipal planners demanded a definitive date although the model supplied only ranges. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Amir published alternative scenarios and explained each source of uncertainty. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. Residents preferred a transparent range of outcomes to reassuring but misleading precision. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
