امة"),EnglishAdvancedWord("transnational perspectives on public policy wording", "المنظورات العابرة للحدود حول صياغة السياسات العامة"),EnglishAdvancedWord("transparent disclosure of public policy wording", "الإفصاح الشفاف عن صياغة السياسات العامة"),EnglishAdvancedWord("systemic vulnerabilities in public policy wording", "الهشاشة البنيوية في صياغة السياسات العامة"),EnglishAdvancedWord("historical contingencies behind public policy wording", "الظروف التاريخية التي شكلت صياغة السياسات العامة"),EnglishAdvancedWord("jurisdictional constraints affecting public policy wording", "قيود الاختصاص التي تؤثر على صياغة السياسات العامة"),EnglishAdvancedWord("critical appraisal of public policy wording", "التقييم التحليلي لـ صياغة السياسات العامة"),EnglishAdvancedWord("burden of justification for public policy wording", "عبء التبرير لـ صياغة السياسات العامة"),EnglishAdvancedWord("competing narratives around public policy wording", "السرديات المتنافسة بشأن صياغة السياسات العامة")],
      grammarTitle:"Reporting verbs and competing viewpoints",
      grammarArabic:"أفعال نقل الآراء وتحديد المواقف",
      grammarExamples:<String>["The director maintained that the procedure had been fair.","The reviewer conceded that the available records were incomplete.","Several participants challenged the underlying assumption about public policy wording."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on public policy wording, Mariam, the legislative editor, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A proposed housing rule promised access for all eligible applicants. A single undefined exception changed who could receive assistance. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Campaigners interpreted fairness differently from the civil servants who drafted the clause. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Mariam commissioned a plain-language revision and a public consultation. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The amended text clarified duties while acknowledging disagreement about the policy itself. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
      listeningQuestion:"What principle guided Mariam's response to the dispute?",
      listeningOptions:<String>["Publish the most dramatic interpretation immediately","Distinguish verified evidence from unresolved interpretations","Exclude every stakeholder who disagrees"],
      listeningAnswer:1,
      readingQuestion:"Why did Mariam resist an immediate definitive answer?",
      readingOptions:<String>["The inquiry did not have any participants","The decision had already been cancelled","The records, assumptions and competing claims required scrutiny"],
