      grammarExamples:<String>["The discrepancy may have arisen during transcription.","The finding cannot by itself prove the allegation.","The witnesses must have interpreted the instruction differently."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on environmental model comparison, Dr. Yusuf, the ecological modeller, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. Two reputable forecasts predicted opposite effects of a proposed reservoir. Satellite imagery showed seasonal changes omitted from one simulation. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Engineers promoted the cheaper forecast while conservationists relied on the worst-case estimate. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Yusuf organised a joint sensitivity analysis using shared datasets. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The final briefing identified decisions that remained robust under either model. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
