      grammarTitle:"Inversion for formal emphasis",
      grammarArabic:"القلب النحوي للتوكيد الرسمي",
      grammarExamples:<String>["Only after the review did the committee reconsider cultural restitution claims.","Rarely had the participants encountered such conflicting records.","Not until the hearing ended did the implications become clear."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on cultural restitution claims, Dr. Farah, the cultural anthropologist, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. An exhibition borrowed sacred objects from a collection acquired generations earlier. Community elders said the artefacts had never been intended for commercial exchange. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. The lending institution invoked legal title while descendants emphasised ongoing spiritual ties. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Farah facilitated talks about stewardship, access and potential restitution. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The agreement recognised that lawful possession and legitimate custodianship need not coincide. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
      listeningQuestion:"What principle guided Dr. Farah's response to the dispute?",
      listeningOptions:<String>["Publish the most dramatic interpretation immediately","Distinguish verified evidence from unresolved interpretations","Exclude every stakeholder who disagrees"],
      listeningAnswer:1,
      readingQuestion:"Why did Dr. Farah resist an immediate definitive answer?",
      readingOptions:<String>["The inquiry did not have any participants","The decision had already been cancelled","The records, assumptions and competing claims required scrutiny"],
      readingAnswer:2,
      writingCue:"By the time the panel published its findings, the ____ was more measured than the original announcement.",
      writingAnswer:"qualified conclusion about cultural restitution claims"),
    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level:"C1",
      number:4,
      unitNumber:2,
      title:"Designing a Fair Public Service",
      titleArabic:"تصميم خدمة عامة عادلة",
      storyTitle:"Designing a Fair Public Service",
      storyTitleArabic:"تصميم خدمة عامة عادلة",
      paragraphs:<String>["At the municipal service centre, Omar, a public service designer, encountered a controversy that had already attracted confident public interpretations. A new digital application reduced queues but excluded citizens without reliable internet. The evidentiary basis for equitable service design seemed persuasive at first, but the historical context of equitable service design complicated the accepted chronology. Rather than treating the interpretive framework for equitable service design as self-explanatory, Omar asked colleagues to identify the methodological assumptions behind equitable service design that informed the institution's language and decisions. The room fell silent when a familiar explanation suddenly appeared less secure.","Service logs showed that older residents abandoned the process disproportionately. During a painstaking examination, the institutional response to equitable service design became as important as the object of the dispute. A detailed examination of the underlying controversy about equitable service design disclosed disagreements that the initial summary had disguised. The preliminary appraisal of equitable service design remained provisional until the team consulted the documentary record on equitable service design and reconstructed the sequence of decisions. What appeared to be a minor technical discrepancy now had implications for the entire inquiry, especially for those previously excluded from it.","Officials celebrated average efficiency while advocates described unequal access. The unresolved tension in equitable service design could not be settled by selecting whichever version sounded most reassuring. One participant emphasised the competing accounts of equitable service design, whereas another pointed to the ethical implications of equitable service design and demanded a more careful distinction between evidence, interpretation and preference. The discussion became uncomfortable precisely because the procedural safeguards for equitable service design required participants to defend the quality of their reasoning rather than the prestige of their institutions. Neither side could simply borrow authority from a title or a credential.","The following week, Omar convened an open session devoted to the public consultation on equitable service design and the regulatory constraints on equitable service design. Omar piloted assisted appointments alongside the online route. The critical assessment of equitable service design was prepared in writing, with explicit references to what had been verified and what still required testing. During the deliberative process around equitable service design, participants were invited to reformulate objections without caricaturing their opponents. The aim was not superficial harmony; it was a decision whose limitations could be explained to a sceptical reader without embarrassment.","By the time the panel published its findings, the qualified conclusion about equitable service design was more measured than the original announcement. The long-term consequences of equitable service design could not be reduced to a triumphant headline, because the judgement imposed practical obligations as well as interpretive restraint. Success was measured by whose needs were met, not simply how fast forms were processed. In her final remarks, Omar argued that intellectual credibility depends not on eliminating every uncertainty but on showing exactly how conclusions follow from the evidence offered. The story ended with a commitment to revisit the decision if new information emerged."],
