      grammarExamples:<String>["Having examined the evidence, the panel reopened the discussion.","Faced with competing accounts, the researchers requested a second review.","The witnesses, questioned independently, offered different explanations."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on equitable service design, Omar, the public service designer, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A new digital application reduced queues but excluded citizens without reliable internet. Service logs showed that older residents abandoned the process disproportionately. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Officials celebrated average efficiency while advocates described unequal access. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Omar piloted assisted appointments alongside the online route. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. Success was measured by whose needs were met, not simply how fast forms were processed. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
