    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level:"C1",
      number:6,
      unitNumber:2,
      title:"When Experts Disagree",
      titleArabic:"عندما يختلف الخبراء",
      storyTitle:"When Experts Disagree",
      storyTitleArabic:"عندما يختلف الخبراء",
      paragraphs:<String>["At the national advisory commission, Dr. Nabil, a evidence synthesis specialist, encountered a controversy that had already attracted confident public interpretations. Two respected specialists offered incompatible explanations for an emerging health pattern. The evidentiary basis for expert disagreement seemed persuasive at first, but the historical context of expert disagreement complicated the accepted chronology. Rather than treating the interpretive framework for expert disagreement as self-explanatory, Dr. Nabil asked colleagues to identify the methodological assumptions behind expert disagreement that informed the institution's language and decisions. The room fell silent when a familiar explanation suddenly appeared less secure.","A methodological appendix revealed that they relied on different inclusion criteria. During a painstaking examination, the institutional response to expert disagreement became as important as the object of the dispute. A detailed examination of the underlying controversy about expert disagreement disclosed disagreements that the initial summary had disguised. The preliminary appraisal of expert disagreement remained provisional until the team consulted the documentary record on expert disagreement and reconstructed the sequence of decisions. What appeared to be a minor technical discrepancy now had implications for the entire inquiry, especially for those previously excluded from it.","Journalists wanted a winner while the panel examined what each study could actually establish. The unresolved tension in expert disagreement could not be settled by selecting whichever version sounded most reassuring. One participant emphasised the competing accounts of expert disagreement, whereas another pointed to the ethical implications of expert disagreement and demanded a more careful distinction between evidence, interpretation and preference. The discussion became uncomfortable precisely because the procedural safeguards for expert disagreement required participants to defend the quality of their reasoning rather than the prestige of their institutions. Neither side could simply borrow authority from a title or a credential.","The following week, Dr. Nabil convened an open session devoted to the public consultation on expert disagreement and the regulatory constraints on expert disagreement. Nabil documented the assumptions and requested a joint reanalysis. The critical assessment of expert disagreement was prepared in writing, with explicit references to what had been verified and what still required testing. During the deliberative process around expert disagreement, participants were invited to reformulate objections without caricaturing their opponents. The aim was not superficial harmony; it was a decision whose limitations could be explained to a sceptical reader without embarrassment.","By the time the panel published its findings, the qualified conclusion about expert disagreement was more measured than the original announcement. The long-term consequences of expert disagreement could not be reduced to a triumphant headline, because the judgement imposed practical obligations as well as interpretive restraint. Their disagreement became useful evidence about the limits of available knowledge. In her final remarks, Dr. Nabil argued that intellectual credibility depends not on eliminating every uncertainty but on showing exactly how conclusions follow from the evidence offered. The story ended with a commitment to revisit the decision if new information emerged."],
