d("transparent disclosure of expert disagreement", "الإفصاح الشفاف عن اختلاف الخبراء"),EnglishAdvancedWord("systemic vulnerabilities in expert disagreement", "الهشاشة البنيوية في اختلاف الخبراء"),EnglishAdvancedWord("historical contingencies behind expert disagreement", "الظروف التاريخية التي شكلت اختلاف الخبراء"),EnglishAdvancedWord("jurisdictional constraints affecting expert disagreement", "قيود الاختصاص التي تؤثر على اختلاف الخبراء"),EnglishAdvancedWord("critical appraisal of expert disagreement", "التقييم التحليلي لـ اختلاف الخبراء"),EnglishAdvancedWord("burden of justification for expert disagreement", "عبء التبرير لـ اختلاف الخبراء"),EnglishAdvancedWord("competing narratives around expert disagreement", "السرديات المتنافسة بشأن اختلاف الخبراء")],
      grammarTitle:"Cleft constructions and focus",
      grammarArabic:"التراكيب التوكيدية وتحديد موضع التركيز",
      grammarExamples:<String>["What the report overlooked was the wider context.","It was the missing document that changed the debate.","What matters most is the distinction between evidence and inference."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on expert disagreement, Dr. Nabil, the evidence synthesis specialist, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. Two respected specialists offered incompatible explanations for an emerging health pattern. A methodological appendix revealed that they relied on different inclusion criteria. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Journalists wanted a winner while the panel examined what each study could actually establish. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Nabil documented the assumptions and requested a joint reanalysis. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. Their disagreement became useful evidence about the limits of available knowledge. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
      listeningQuestion:"What principle guided Dr. Nabil's response to the dispute?",
      listeningOptions:<String>["Publish the most dramatic interpretation immediately","Distinguish verified evidence from unresolved interpretations","Exclude every stakeholder who disagrees"],
      listeningAnswer:1,
      readingQuestion:"Why did Dr. Nabil resist an immediate definitive answer?",
      readingOptions:<String>["The inquiry did not have any participants","The decision had already been cancelled","The records, assumptions and competing claims required scrutiny"],
      readingAnswer:2,
      writingCue:"By the time the panel published its findings, the ____ was more measured than the original announcement.",
      writingAnswer:"qualified conclusion about expert disagreement"),
    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level:"C1",
      number:7,
      unitNumber:2,
      title:"The International Arts Symposium",
      titleArabic:"الندوة الدولية للفنون",
      storyTitle:"The International Arts Symposium",
      storyTitleArabic:"الندوة الدولية للفنون",
      paragraphs:<String>["At the international arts institute, Yara, a symposium curator, encountered a controversy that had already attracted confident public interpretations. An acclaimed exhibition invited artists whose histories of displacement differed markedly. The evidentiary basis for transnational arts dialogue seemed persuasive at first, but the historical context of transnational arts dialogue complicated the accepted chronology. Rather than treating the interpretive framework for transnational arts dialogue as self-explanatory, Yara asked colleagues to identify the methodological assumptions behind transnational arts dialogue that informed the institution's language and decisions. The room fell silent when a familiar explanation suddenly appeared less secure.","A promotional essay reduced several conflicting experiences to one universal narrative. During a painstaking examination, the institutional response to transnational arts dialogue became as important as the object of the dispute. A detailed examination of the underlying controversy about transnational arts dialogue disclosed disagreements that the initial summary had disguised. The preliminary appraisal of transnational arts dialogue remained provisional until the team consulted the documentary record on transnational arts dialogue and reconstructed the sequence of decisions. What appeared to be a minor technical discrepancy now had implications for the entire inquiry, especially for those previously excluded from it.","Participants objected that the framing erased political and linguistic complexity. The unresolved tension in transnational arts dialogue could not be settled by selecting whichever version sounded most reassuring. One participant emphasised the competing accounts of transnational arts dialogue, whereas another pointed to the ethical implications of transnational arts dialogue and demanded a more careful distinction between evidence, interpretation and preference. The discussion became uncomfortable precisely because the procedural safeguards for transnational arts dialogue required participants to defend the quality of their reasoning rather than the prestige of their institutions. Neither side could simply borrow authority from a title or a credential.","The following week, Yara convened an open session devoted to the public consultation on transnational arts dialogue and the regulatory constraints on transnational arts dialogue. Yara redesigned the sessions around moderated, multilingual dialogue. The critical assessment of transnational arts dialogue was prepared in writing, with explicit references to what had been verified and what still required testing. During the deliberative process around transnational arts dialogue, participants were invited to reformulate objections without caricaturing their opponents. The aim was not superficial harmony; it was a decision whose limitations could be explained to a sceptical reader without embarrassment.","By the time the panel published its findings, the qualified conclusion about transnational arts dialogue was more measured than the original announcement. The long-term consequences of transnational arts dialogue could not be reduced to a triumphant headline, because the judgement imposed practical obligations as well as interpretive restraint. The symposium valued disagreement as an invitation to interpret responsibly. In her final remarks, Yara argued that intellectual credibility depends not on eliminating every uncertainty but on showing exactly how conclusions follow from the evidence offered. The story ended with a commitment to revisit the decision if new information emerged."],
