national arts dialogue", "المراجعة المستقلة لـ الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات"),EnglishAdvancedWord("policy implications of transnational arts dialogue", "الآثار على السياسات العامة لـ الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات"),EnglishAdvancedWord("transnational perspectives on transnational arts dialogue", "المنظورات العابرة للحدود حول الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات"),EnglishAdvancedWord("transparent disclosure of transnational arts dialogue", "الإفصاح الشفاف عن الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات"),EnglishAdvancedWord("systemic vulnerabilities in transnational arts dialogue", "الهشاشة البنيوية في الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات"),EnglishAdvancedWord("historical contingencies behind transnational arts dialogue", "الظروف التاريخية التي شكلت الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات"),EnglishAdvancedWord("jurisdictional constraints affecting transnational arts dialogue", "قيود الاختصاص التي تؤثر على الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات"),EnglishAdvancedWord("critical appraisal of transnational arts dialogue", "التقييم التحليلي لـ الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات"),EnglishAdvancedWord("burden of justification for transnational arts dialogue", "عبء التبرير لـ الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات"),EnglishAdvancedWord("competing narratives around transnational arts dialogue", "السرديات المتنافسة بشأن الحوار الفني العابر للثقافات")],
      grammarTitle:"Reporting verbs and competing viewpoints",
      grammarArabic:"أفعال نقل الآراء وتحديد المواقف",
      grammarExamples:<String>["The director maintained that the procedure had been fair.","The reviewer conceded that the available records were incomplete.","Several participants challenged the underlying assumption about transnational arts dialogue."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on transnational arts dialogue, Yara, the symposium curator, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. An acclaimed exhibition invited artists whose histories of displacement differed markedly. A promotional essay reduced several conflicting experiences to one universal narrative. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Participants objected that the framing erased political and linguistic complexity. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Yara redesigned the sessions around moderated, multilingual dialogue. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The symposium valued disagreement as an invitation to interpret responsibly. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
