      grammarTitle:"Cohesive devices and qualified conclusions",
      grammarArabic:"الروابط الحجاجية والاستنتاج المتحفظ",
      grammarExamples:<String>["The figures are incomplete; consequently, the inference is provisional.","The records disagree; nonetheless, a cautious assessment is possible.","The result is informative, provided that its limitations are disclosed."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on institutional accountability reform, Dr. Sami, the governance auditor, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. Annual compliance reports presented perfect scores despite persistent service failures. Anonymous testimony suggested that staff were rewarded for avoiding bad news. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Executives equated procedural compliance with meaningful responsibility. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Sami designed independent grievance reviews and publication of corrective actions. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The institution came to treat accountability as continuing scrutiny, not an annual ceremony. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
