      grammarExamples:<String>["What the report overlooked was the wider context.","It was the missing document that changed the debate.","What matters most is the distinction between evidence and inference."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on cross-cultural diplomatic negotiation, Dalia, the international negotiator, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. Delegates interpreted a polite expression of agreement as a binding commitment. The official minutes recorded no shared definition of the disputed phrase. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. One delegation demanded immediate enforcement while another described a provisional understanding. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Dalia arranged a mediated clarification before new concessions were drafted. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The revised accord distinguished diplomatic courtesy from enforceable promises. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
