      grammarExamples:<String>["The director maintained that the procedure had been fair.","The reviewer conceded that the available records were incomplete.","Several participants challenged the underlying assumption about macroeconomic forecasting limits."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on macroeconomic forecasting limits, Dr. Tarek, the macroeconomic analyst, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A forecast of rapid growth became the basis for an ambitious spending programme. Revised employment figures revealed how sensitive the model was to migration assumptions. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Ministers wanted a single estimate while analysts warned against false precision. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Tarek published probability ranges and stress-tested alternative policy choices. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The briefing made uncertainty visible without abandoning decisions altogether. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
