      grammarTitle:"Calibrated modality and epistemic stance",
      grammarArabic:"درجات الاحتمال والموقف المعرفي",
      grammarExamples:<String>["The discrepancy may have arisen during transcription.","The finding cannot by itself prove the allegation.","The witnesses must have interpreted the instruction differently."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on science in public deliberation, Dr. Amal, the science-policy liaison, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A technical report was used as a political slogan during a heated council debate. Its conclusion contained qualifications omitted from campaign materials. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Researchers resisted partisan misuse while citizens demanded accessible explanations. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Amal hosted a public evidence hearing with transparent questions. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The session treated scientific expertise as guidance for democratic choice rather than its substitute. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
