      grammarExamples:<String>["The claim that the record was complete, which few had questioned, proved misleading.","What the committee understood the witnesses to mean remains contested.","The objection raised by those whose evidence was excluded deserves attention."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on argumentative architecture, Professor Adel, the philosopher of language, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A persuasive essay defended two premises that undermined one another. Footnotes disclosed an unstated definition on which the conclusion depended. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Supporters defended the rhetoric while sceptics challenged the inference. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Adel reconstructed the argument as a transparent sequence of claims and warrants. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The revision sacrificed theatrical certainty to gain genuine logical coherence. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
