      grammarExamples:<String>["Calling the omission an oversight understated its importance.","The apparently reassuring conclusion was strikingly evasive.","A more restrained formulation would have conveyed the qualification."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on historical moral judgment, Professor Tariq, the historian of ethics, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A national award sparked demands to condemn a long-deceased reformer. Private letters revealed convictions at odds with the reformer's public work. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Activists sought moral clarity while some historians warned against anachronism. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Tariq distinguished explanation, mitigation and justification in the archival review. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The resulting essay held the past answerable without pretending historical actors shared today's categories. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
