      grammarExamples:<String>["This is not to suggest that every account is equally persuasive.","The stronger claim, however, exceeds what the evidence can sustain.","The argument is compelling only insofar as its premises are accepted."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on epistemic certainty limits, Dr. Sameer, the epistemologist, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A consensus statement converted high confidence into the language of inevitability. Its supporting studies contained unresolved measurement disagreements. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Institutional leaders feared that acknowledging doubt would appear weak. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Sameer drafted a graduated account of confidence and residual error. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The final statement demonstrated why disciplined uncertainty is not intellectual indecision. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
