      grammarExamples:<String>["The minister's remark implied consent without explicitly granting it.","An apparently neutral term concealed an evaluative presupposition.","The ambiguity in strategic semantic ambiguity was productive rather than accidental."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on strategic semantic ambiguity, Dr. Saif, the discourse analyst, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A treaty clause appeared to satisfy negotiating parties with opposing expectations. Early drafts showed that an ambiguous verb had been retained intentionally. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Negotiators defended flexibility while legal scholars warned of future conflict. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Saif compared the competing pragmatic interpretations in context. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The study distinguished constructive flexibility from evasive language that postpones responsibility. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
