      grammarExamples:<String>["Under no circumstances should archival silence be equated with proof.","Only rarely does a conclusion survive every counterexample.","Not until the definitions were compared did the disagreement emerge."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on expert authority legitimacy, Dr. Kamal, the sociologist of expertise, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. Experts issued a recommendation that affected communities had not been invited to question. A consultation log exposed the absence of local testimony. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Officials cited credentials while residents demanded accountable reasoning. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Kamal proposed a review combining technical competence with participatory scrutiny. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The revised process recognised that authority must be earned through transparency as well as expertise. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
