      grammarExamples:<String>["Calling the omission an oversight understated its importance.","The apparently reassuring conclusion was strikingly evasive.","A more restrained formulation would have conveyed the qualification."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on model assumption critique, Dr. Basil, the computational epistemologist, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A widely used algorithm ranked communities by apparent vulnerability. Inspection revealed a proxy variable that reproduced historic exclusion. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Developers defended predictive accuracy while affected residents disputed the categories. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Basil subjected the model to counterfactual and fairness tests. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The review asked not merely whether predictions worked but whose reality the model represented. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
