ribution", "التواضع المعرفي إزاء نسبة الأعمال الفنية إلى أصحابها"),EnglishAdvancedWord("reasoned dissent concerning artistic authorship attribution", "المعارضة القائمة على الحجة بشأن نسبة الأعمال الفنية إلى أصحابها"),EnglishAdvancedWord("hermeneutic restraint in artistic authorship attribution", "التحفظ التأويلي عند نسبة الأعمال الفنية إلى أصحابها")],
      grammarTitle:"Ellipsis and substitution in sustained arguments",
      grammarArabic:"الحذف والإحلال لتحقيق التماسك",
      grammarExamples:<String>["One witness endorsed the conclusion; the other did not.","Some accepted the initial premise, whereas others rejected it.","The second interpretation is no less plausible than the first."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on artistic authorship attribution, Dr. Sara, the art historian, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A newly exhibited painting was attributed to a major artist on stylistic grounds. Material analysis suggested collaboration with an undocumented apprentice. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Collectors prized a famous name while researchers challenged the single-author narrative. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Sara documented the evidence and revised the exhibition label. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The investigation showed how attribution shapes both cultural meaning and economic value. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
      listeningQuestion:"What principle guided Dr. Sara's response to the dispute?",
      listeningOptions:<String>["Publish the most dramatic interpretation immediately","Distinguish verified evidence from unresolved interpretations","Exclude every stakeholder who disagrees"],
      listeningAnswer:1,
      readingQuestion:"Why did Dr. Sara resist an immediate definitive answer?",
      readingOptions:<String>["The inquiry did not have any participants","The decision had already been cancelled","The records, assumptions and competing claims required scrutiny"],
      readingAnswer:2,
      writingCue:"By the time the panel published its findings, the ____ was more measured than the original announcement.",
      writingAnswer:"qualified conclusion about artistic authorship attribution"),
    EnglishAdvancedLesson(
      level:"C2",
      number:6,
      unitNumber:3,
      title:"Reconstructing a Complex Debate",
      titleArabic:"إعادة بناء مناظرة معقدة",
      storyTitle:"Reconstructing a Complex Debate",
      storyTitleArabic:"إعادة بناء مناظرة معقدة",
      paragraphs:<String>["At the public policy archive, Dr. Hisham, a argumentation scholar, encountered a controversy that had already attracted confident public interpretations. A decades-old debate was remembered through one widely quoted speech. The evidentiary basis for complex debate reconstruction seemed persuasive at first, but the historical context of complex debate reconstruction complicated the accepted chronology. Rather than treating the interpretive framework for complex debate reconstruction as self-explanatory, Dr. Hisham asked colleagues to identify the methodological assumptions behind complex debate reconstruction that informed the institution's language and decisions. The room fell silent when a familiar explanation suddenly appeared less secure.","The full transcript revealed objections that later summaries had omitted. During a painstaking examination, the institutional response to complex debate reconstruction became as important as the object of the dispute. A detailed examination of the underlying controversy about complex debate reconstruction disclosed disagreements that the initial summary had disguised. The preliminary appraisal of complex debate reconstruction remained provisional until the team consulted the documentary record on complex debate reconstruction and reconstructed the sequence of decisions. What appeared to be a minor technical discrepancy now had implications for the entire inquiry, especially for those previously excluded from it.","Commentators treated the famous exchange as a decisive victory. The unresolved tension in complex debate reconstruction could not be settled by selecting whichever version sounded most reassuring. One participant emphasised the competing accounts of complex debate reconstruction, whereas another pointed to the ethical implications of complex debate reconstruction and demanded a more careful distinction between evidence, interpretation and preference. The discussion became uncomfortable precisely because the procedural safeguards for complex debate reconstruction required participants to defend the quality of their reasoning rather than the prestige of their institutions. Neither side could simply borrow authority from a title or a credential.","The following week, Dr. Hisham convened an open session devoted to the public consultation on complex debate reconstruction and the regulatory constraints on complex debate reconstruction. Hisham reconstructed competing premises and shifts in audience response. The critical assessment of complex debate reconstruction was prepared in writing, with explicit references to what had been verified and what still required testing. During the deliberative process around complex debate reconstruction, participants were invited to reformulate objections without caricaturing their opponents. The aim was not superficial harmony; it was a decision whose limitations could be explained to a sceptical reader without embarrassment.","By the time the panel published its findings, the qualified conclusion about complex debate reconstruction was more measured than the original announcement. The long-term consequences of complex debate reconstruction could not be reduced to a triumphant headline, because the judgement imposed practical obligations as well as interpretive restraint. His analysis showed that an argument's history is rarely identical to its popular afterlife. In her final remarks, Dr. Hisham argued that intellectual credibility depends not on eliminating every uncertainty but on showing exactly how conclusions follow from the evidence offered. The story ended with a commitment to revisit the decision if new information emerged.","Looking back, Dr. Hisham recognised the epistemic ambiguity in complex debate reconstruction as a central feature of the dispute, not an inconvenient flaw awaiting a clever rhetorical cure. The rhetorical subtext of complex debate reconstruction continued to shape how observers narrated the outcome: some praised the compromise, others criticised its caution, and still others questioned the categories through which the argument had been posed. None of these perspectives deserved automatic immunity from examination. A genuinely exacting account had to preserve the difference between a persuasive formulation and a proposition that could withstand sustained counterargument."],
