      grammarTitle:"Causality, agency and nominalised processes",
      grammarArabic:"السببية والفاعل والعمليات الاسمية",
      grammarExamples:<String>["The correlation did not warrant an attribution of cause.","The decision was framed as inevitable, obscuring who had made it.","Attribution of responsibility requires more than temporal succession."],
      listening:"In a specialist seminar on interpretive authority politics, Dr. Inas, the critical theory scholar, explained why an early institutional statement required reconsideration. A government exhibition described a disputed historical event using one approved term. Alternative labels carried different implications for recognition and responsibility. A second participant pointed out that apparently accurate documents still needed contextual interpretation. Officials claimed neutrality while historians demonstrated how naming framed judgment. The discussion turned from the search for a decisive slogan to the difficult work of comparing sources, exposing assumptions, and allowing relevant objections to be heard. Inas convened a multilingual panel to examine the competing vocabularies. The audience learned that a defensible judgment need not pretend to be infallible. The debate exposed interpretation as a public exercise of power rather than a private preference. The final recommendation was therefore to distinguish verified observations from interpretive claims, document residual uncertainty, and make the reasoning accessible to those affected.",
      listeningQuestion:"What principle guided Dr. Inas's response to the dispute?",
      listeningOptions:<String>["Publish the most dramatic interpretation immediately","Distinguish verified evidence from unresolved interpretations","Exclude every stakeholder who disagrees"],
      listeningAnswer:1,
      readingQuestion:"Why did Dr. Inas resist an immediate definitive answer?",
      readingOptions:<String>["The inquiry did not have any participants","The decision had already been cancelled","The records, assumptions and competing claims required scrutiny"],
      readingAnswer:2,
      writingCue:"By the time the panel published its findings, the ____ was more measured than the original announcement.",
      writingAnswer:"qualified conclusion about interpretive authority politics"),
